            <h2>Helpful Planning Notes</h2>
            <h3>Ask the care team what equipment is appropriate.</h3>
            <p>Comfort Care can help with rental availability and product options, but equipment choice should follow guidance from the patient's medical provider, discharge planner, physical therapist, or care team.</p>
            <h3>Confirm insurance and Medicare details directly.</h3>
            <p>Coverage, documentation, supplier rules, and reimbursement can vary. Use Medicare.gov or your insurance plan for official coverage guidance.</p>
            <h3>Measure the home before delivery.</h3>
            <p>Doorways, hallways, bedroom space, bathroom access, stairs, and elevator access can affect which equipment works best at home.</p>
